    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23eddj9am1nebvkG14YLgqW)_\n\n**Problem:** at startup, while vulpea indexed the vault, the echo area intermittently showed `redisplay--pre-redisplay-functions: (wrong-type-argument number-or-marker-p nil)`. Sia's backtrace: `cursor-sensor-tangible-pos` returned nil inside `cursor-sensor--move-to-tangible` on the Dashboard window. `cursor-intangible-mode` was on while the dashboard was erased or half-built, so no button existed to move point to.\n\n**Changes**\n- `sp-dashboard`: `sp-dashboard--isolate-menu` no longer calls `cursor-intangible-mode`. A new `sp-dashboard--enable-intangible` turns it on from an idle timer (0.1 s) after the draw, and only if the buffer is live and has a button. The property marking and the keymap overlay are unchanged.\n- `sp-vulpea-base`: `vulpea-db-sync-scan-on-enable` is nil, so enabling `vulpea-db-autosync-mode` no longer scans the vault at startup (the database, save hook and watchers still work; an empty database is still scanned). `sp-vulpea-scan-once` runs `vulpea-db-sync-full-scan` two idle seconds after the first tracked note is opened, then removes itself. `M-x vulpea-db-sync-full-scan` still works by hand.\n- The literate docs (`sp-dashboard.org`, `sp-vulpea.org`) are updated with the code.\n\n**Not tested:** no Emacs in this environment, so none of this was run. `vulpea-db-sync-scan-on-enable` and `vulpea-db-sync-tracked-file-p` come from reading vulpea's source on GitHub; check they exist in the installed version.\n\nNo CHANGELOG entry: #83 rewrites the file, so an entry here would conflict. Add it after #83 merges.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01U17WoSwrRGjp7q9svv9TBQ)_",
