                "message": "Defer the vulpea scan and start cursor-intangible after the dashboard is drawn\n\nvulpea-db-sync-scan-on-enable is nil, and a one-shot find-file-hook runs\nvulpea-db-sync-full-scan once the first vault note is opened. The dashboard\nenables cursor-intangible-mode from an idle timer, only when the buffer has\na button, so the redisplay hook no longer signals wrong-type-argument on a\nhalf-built buffer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U17WoSwrRGjp7q9svv9TBQ",
